WEBVTT

00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:08.625
(Hunter) Tomorrow,
we will arrive to Rumi Rock.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.750
- So, a toast...
- (Paddington slurping)

00:00:15.417 --> 00:00:16.250
Mmm!

00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:20.000
Oh, excuse me.

00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:23.334
- ...to finding Aunt Lucy.
- Hear hear!

00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:26.417
- Well, it's certainly interesting.
- (Mrs Brown) Mmm! Mmm!

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:31.167
So, uh...

00:00:31.292 --> 00:00:34.167
- tell me, young bear...
- Hmm!

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:37.375
...why was your aunt so interested
in Rumi Rock?

00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:40.125
We don't know, Mr Hunter.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.209
The Reverend Mother said
she was looking for something.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.959
She was wasting her time.

00:00:44.084 --> 00:00:46.584
Rumi Rock is just a bunch of old stones.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:51.625
A bunch of old stones that,
according to legend,

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.500
is the first step to finding...
El Dorado.

00:00:56.584 --> 00:00:59.084
What? You mean...

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:01.084
- Hmm!
- (Electricity crackling)

00:01:01.209 --> 00:01:02.584
Nice chips!

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:07.459
- He means the mythical lost city, not...
- Oh. Right.

00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:10.625
When the Spanish invaders came,

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.750
they found all the treasures of Peru,
except for one.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.625
The most precious treasure of all.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.542
Hmm?

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:24.084
The gold which the Incas valued
more than anything else.

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:27.459
But it could not be found.

00:01:27.584 --> 00:01:35.042
And this is because the Incas entrusted it
to "Los Espiritus del Bosque".

00:01:36.709 --> 00:01:39.917
The spirits of the jungle

00:01:40.042 --> 00:01:44.417
who promised to keep it secret
and hidden in the forest forever.

00:01:46.209 --> 00:01:50.042
Now... that's El Dorado.

00:01:51.709 --> 00:01:57.709
So, are you suggesting that
Aunt Lucy was looking for El Dorado?

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:00.334
Aren't we all?

00:02:00.459 --> 00:02:02.625
In our own ways.

00:02:03.584 --> 00:02:04.584
No?

00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:09.709
But why would she be looking
for El Dorado, Mrs Brown?

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.542
She has no interest in gold.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.209
Let's not get carried away with...
(Chuckles)

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.542
...some old pictures in a book.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:19.834
If El Dorado exists,
why has no one found it?

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:23.250
Because none of them had... this.

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:28.167
It is said the only clue
the Incas left

00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:31.459
to where the spirits of the jungle
hid the gold

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.250
was in a special bracelet.

00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:38.500
- A bracelet... like this!
- Ooh!

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.792
(Mary gasps)

00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.459
Where did you get that?

00:02:42.584 --> 00:02:44.250
It's Aunt Lucy's.

00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:45.542
She always wore it.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:49.334
And it is the key to finding El Dorado
and all its treasures.

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:51.167
- Wow!
- (Scoffs)

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:55.417
There's no reason why Aunt Lucy
would have an ancient Inca bracelet.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:58.500
- But she did! Look! It's the same!
- It may very well look the same.

00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:00.542
Honestly, Henry,
you're really taking the fun out of this.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:05.917
- It's just an ordinary stringy bracelet.
- It's not an ordinary bracelet. It is...

00:03:06.042 --> 00:03:07.459
- (Paddington grunting)
- Oh!

00:03:07.584 --> 00:03:10.167
(Paddington) I'm OK.
Nothing broken.

00:03:13.542 --> 00:03:15.667
- ...Quipu.
- Quip-who?

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.750
An ancient Incan knot language

00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:22.042
used for secret messages,
hidden in riddles.

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:27.375
So, if we work out what this says,
it might help us find Aunt Lucy?

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:31.792
Lend me this bracelet for a few hours.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.959
I may be able to translate it.

00:03:35.084 --> 00:03:38.917
Everyone who searches
for El Dorado dies.

00:03:43.042 --> 00:03:48.250
Then... we can't let that happen
to Aunt Lucy.

00:03:49.042 --> 00:03:51.334
Hmm... (Chuckles)

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:55.584
(Judy) 'Later came the Spanish conquest
of the Incas,

00:03:55.709 --> 00:03:57.917
'and with them the gold hunters.

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:04.000
'The greediest of all
was Gonzalo Caboto.'

00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:05.500
(Spraying)

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:09.250
Ugh! What is that smell?

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:11.750
Gotta smell good in the jungle,
you know?

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:14.292
- (Mrs Brown) Night night, guys!
- Night.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:16.292
- (Judy) Night.
- Love you!

00:04:17.292 --> 00:04:19.459
Clear. No spiders under here.

00:04:19.584 --> 00:04:21.292
(Paddington) Night night, Mrs Brown!

00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:22.834
(Mrs Brown) Night, Paddington.

00:04:22.959 --> 00:04:24.667
Looks simple enough.

00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:28.042
Mmm...

00:04:30.125 --> 00:04:31.875
Mmm... ooh!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.334
Uh-uh...

00:04:33.459 --> 00:04:35.042
Oh...!

00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:42.750
Now, the trick with a hammock
is not to let it see you... coming!

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:44.667
Whoa! Ugh!

00:04:45.459 --> 00:04:47.792
(Grunting)

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:50.500
Nice hammock...
Steady! Steady! Ugh!

00:04:51.292 --> 00:04:54.709
There we go.
It's not as comfortable...

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.417
(Grunting)

00:04:56.542 --> 00:04:58.042
Argh!

00:04:58.917 --> 00:05:00.250
(Mumbles)

00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:02.209
(Snoring)

00:05:16.917 --> 00:05:19.584
- What does it say?
- It doesn't make any sense.

00:05:19.709 --> 00:05:21.834
- Why not?
- Cos it's a riddle!

00:05:21.959 --> 00:05:24.209
- Who are you talking to?
- Uh-oh!

00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:26.917
No one.

00:05:27.042 --> 00:05:29.750
You're seeing the ghosts again,
aren't you?

00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:32.959
Gina... I'm fine.

00:05:34.375 --> 00:05:36.667
But you made me a promise.

00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:39.750
- We don't need gold.
- And... And you are right,

00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:43.542
but if we had it,
we could buy a real house

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:46.959
- with stairs and beds and square windows!
- Papa!

00:05:47.084 --> 00:05:49.750
We could bring honour on the family.

00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:51.959
But we only need each other,

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.500
and I'm scared
I'm going to lose you again,

00:05:55.625 --> 00:05:57.000
for good this time.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:03.292
Please... turn the boat around.

00:06:05.584 --> 00:06:08.417
Don't listen to her!
She doesn't understand.

00:06:08.542 --> 00:06:10.334
We need the gold! The glory!

00:06:10.459 --> 00:06:11.917
Right!

00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:17.209
- Let's turn the boat round right now!
- You mean it?

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:20.792
You are my treasure, and I love you.

00:06:20.917 --> 00:06:23.917
Go untie the mooring rope.
Go! Go! Go!

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:28.917
<i>Valiente idiota. ¡Nunca!</i>

00:06:29.542 --> 00:06:32.125
You were never a Cabot.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.709
Never!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.959
I'm proud of you, Papa.

00:06:38.584 --> 00:06:41.292
This could be
a whole new chapter in our...

00:06:43.084 --> 00:06:44.125
Papa?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.667
- I love you, Gina...
- Papa!

00:06:45.792 --> 00:06:47.959
...but I have to get that gold.
I have to!

00:06:48.084 --> 00:06:49.667
You double-crossing pig!
<i>Mentiroso!</i>

00:06:49.792 --> 00:06:51.750
I am doing this for the both of us!

00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:54.500
I promise I'll come back for you
tomorrow!

00:06:54.625 --> 00:06:56.959
(Gina) Argh! Papa!

00:06:57.084 --> 00:07:00.084
You can't even drive that boat
without me!

00:07:00.875 --> 00:07:02.459
Wow!

00:07:02.584 --> 00:07:04.292
I think she took that well.

00:07:04.417 --> 00:07:06.875
And you...
You had me there!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Maybe you're not a failure
after all, you know?

00:07:11.125 --> 00:07:13.417
All right!
We have some work to do.

00:07:14.084 --> 00:07:15.209
(Creaking)

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.334
What's that creaking noise?

00:07:17.959 --> 00:07:19.667
Boom!

